| Layer | Choice | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Host: server, scheduler, KV manager, loaders, metrics, UI server, CLI | **Rust** (stable, edition 2021) | Native speed, zero-cost abstractions, fearless concurrency for scheduler/KV, and easy FFI to C kernels. No GC pauses during serving. |
| Kernel ABI | **C (extern "C")** | Universal interop. CUDA, HIP, Metal, SYCL, and Rust can all call C. No C++ name mangling issues. Simple header-based contract. |
| Kernel Implementation | **C/CUDA/HIP/Metal** | Direct hardware access. No Python overhead. Each platform gets a native implementation. |
| Reference/Testing | **Python (NumPy/JAX)** |
